  "question": {
    "text": "The potential energy of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> particle, free to move along the <em>x</em>-axis, is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>J</mtext></math>. The total mechanical energy of the particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> then, the maximum speed (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) is",
